      "refersTo": "overview",
      "description": "Divided summary counts in one white surface.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-overview\"><div><strong>12</strong><span>Open opportunities</span></div><div><strong>4</strong><span>Upcoming cycles</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>Dates within 14 days</span></div><div><strong>24</strong><span>Total tracked</span></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-overview{font-family:\"Avenir Next\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:22px 8px}.ds-overview>div{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:0 26px;border-right:1px solid var(--line)}.ds-overview>div:last-child{border:0}.ds-overview strong{font-size:32px;color:var(--navy);font-weight:550;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-overview span{font-size:14px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-overview{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;padding:8px 0}.ds-overview>div{padding:14px 17px;border:0;gap:12px}.ds-overview>div:nth-child(odd){border-right:1px solid var(--line)}.ds-overview>div:nth-child(-n+2){border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.ds-overview strong{font-size:27px}.ds-overview span{font-size:12px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Attached evidence",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "evidence",
      "description": "Wash region for progressively disclosed source evidence.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-evidence\" aria-label=\"Opportunity evidence\"><div class=\"ds-evidence-head\"><h3>Official opportunity title</h3><a href=\"#official-call\">Read official call <svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12 12 4M4 4h8v8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg></a></div><div class=\"ds-evidence-grid\"><div><h4>Eligibility</h4><p>Requirements and submission conditions.</p></div><div><h4>Evidence &amp; verification limits</h4><p>Source-linked findings and review limitations.</p></div></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-evidence{font-family:\"Avenir Next\",\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;padding:26px 30px;background:var(--wash);border-top:1px solid var(--line);animation:ds-detail-in 220ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)}.ds-evidence-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;align-items:start;margin-bottom:22px}.ds-evidence h3{margin:0;color:var(--ink);font-size:18px;line-height:1.35}.ds-evidence a{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;color:var(--teal);text-underline-offset:4px}.ds-evidence a:hover{text-decoration-thickness:2px}.ds-evidence a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:3px}.ds-evidence-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:28px 42px}.ds-evidence h4{font-size:12px;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 7px}.ds-evidence p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);margin:0;max-width:72ch}@keyframes ds-detail-in{from{clip-path:inset(0 0 12%)}to{clip-path:inset(0)}}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-evidence{padding:22px 18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:0 0 12px 12px}.ds-evidence-head{display:block}.ds-evidence h3{font-size:16px;margin-bottom:13px}.ds-evidence-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:22px}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-evidence{animation:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The research ledger",
    "overview": "The research ledger translates the established Ividence paper, navy, and teal identity into a compact workspace for comparing opportunities. Editorial Georgia headings give the page its character; the Avenir Next / Segoe UI interface carries the dense evidence and controls.\n\nWhite records and pale wash panels sit on warm paper. Thin dividers organize the information, while navy anchors the page and teal marks links. Information expands in place so the shortlist remains the point of reference.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper with navy structure and restrained teal links.",
      "Compact records with progressively disclosed evidence.",
      "Tabular numbers for ranks, dates, counts, and scores.",
      "Stacked mobile records with full-width evidence."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Evidence in Place Rule",
        "body": "Keep expanded evidence attached to its opportunity and visually subordinate through the wash surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Editorial Accent Rule",
        "body": "Use Georgia for editorial headings; use the interface sans stack for controls, records, labels, and data.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Divider First Rule",
        "body": "Separate records and sections with thin strokes and surface tones rather than shadows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep opportunity titles operable as disclosure buttons with visible focus and expanded state.",
      "Do pair every availability color with its written status.",
      "Do preserve tabular numerals for aligned ranks, dates, scores, and summary counts.",
      "Do keep mobile evidence full width and stack its sections into one column.",
      "Do label the initial comparison as a baseline and preserve the distinction between official evidence and research assessments.",
      "Do disable disclosure animation and smooth scrolling when reduced motion is requested."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use status color alone to convey availability or change.",
      "Don't turn every record into a floating card on desktop; keep the compact, divided table.",
      "Don't replace the established SVG symbols with text glyph icons.",
      "Don't apply the editorial heading face to controls or dense evidence."
    ]
  }
}
